wirust uses the `fingerprint` crate of mirrust (https://github.com/dec0iiyy/mirrust),
licensed under GPL-3.0-only. Its known-client dataset, compiled into the binary, holds
fingerprints taken from the BSD-3-Clause licensed uTLS
(https://github.com/refraction-networking/utls) and from the MIT licensed test signatures
of curl-impersonate (https://github.com/lexiforest/curl-impersonate, copyright (c)
curl_cffi developers).

The other Rust crates linked into the binary are under permissive licences (MIT,
Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, CDLA-Permissive-2.0), except
`option-ext`, which is MPL-2.0 and used unmodified. Their copyright notices and licence texts are in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md, which ships with every
release archive.
